          >
            Worldwide
          </h2>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-image
          border-radius="10px"
          padding="10px 12px"
          width="600px"
          src="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
          alt="REPLACE_ME"
          href="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/"
        />
        <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
          <p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇷🇺 Russia - Drone strike. </strong>Russia launched a large overnight missile and drone assault across Ukraine, killing at least 16 people and injuring dozens in strikes that hit civilian areas in Kyiv, Odesa, and Dnipro. In Kyiv, four people, including a 12-year-old child, were killed. Odesa suffered at least nine deaths, and Dnipro saw two killed and 27 injured, five critically. Ukrainian authorities warned the toll could rise as rescue efforts continued. Ukraine’s air force said it intercepted 31 missiles and 636 drones (<a href="https://www.dw.com/en/several-killed-in-russian-strikes-across-ukraine-many-more-injured/a-76803204" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">missile terror</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇨🇳 China - Xi met Russian officials.</strong> China’s President Xi Jinping met Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov in Beijing and called for “closer and stronger strategic coordination” between China and Russia. Xi said both countries should defend their interests and protect the unity of the Global South amid global instability. Lavrov said Russia could help offset China’s energy shortages (<a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/15/chinas-xi-meets-russian-fm-lavrov-calls-relations-with-moscow-precious" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">axis tightened</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇿🇦 South Africa - Appoints US ambassador. </strong>South African President Cyril Ramaphosa has appointed Roelf Meyer as the country’s ambassador to the US, filling a post that had been vacant since Ebrahim Rasool was expelled last year. Meyer, 78, is a former minister in South Africa’s last apartheid-era government and later became a key negotiator in the talks that ended apartheid alongside Ramaphosa (<a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cwyjjjz8n8ko" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">tactical pick</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇮🇳 India - Voter list concern.</strong> More than 9Mn people in West Bengal have lost voting rights after the Election Commission of India completed a controversial voter roll revision ahead of the state’s April 23 and 29 assembly polls. Many affected voters, especially Muslims and women, say their names were removed over spelling mismatches, nickname differences, missing residential proof, or post-marriage surname changes, even after voting in past elections (<a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/16/muslims-the-target-fury-as-millions-lose-voting-rights-in-indias-bengal" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">deleted voices</a>).
</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
