            Foundations
          </h2>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text
  padding="10px 12px"
  font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;"
  color="#000000"
>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 500; margin: 0;">
    How was modern China founded?
  </h2>
</mj-text>
<mj-image
  border="1px solid #00000013"
  border-radius="10px"
  padding="10px 12px"
  width="600px"
  src="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
  alt="REPLACE_ME"
  href="https://www.geopoliticalsummary.com/"
/>

<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Background: </strong>Modern China was officially founded on October 1, 1949, when Mao Zedong declared the establishment of the People’s Republic of China (PRC) in Beijing. Sun Yat-sen and the Nationalist Party’s revolutionary efforts led to the <a href="https://history.state.gov/milestones/1899-1913/chinese-rev" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">end of the Qing dynasty in 1912</a>. However, corruption and weak control provided a gateway for foreign exploitation, especially by Japan, whose invasions devastated China.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">During this period, Mao Zedong’s Communists gained strength through guerrilla tactics and peasant support. After World War II, the civil war between the Nationalists and the Communists resumed. By 1949, the Communists defeated the Nationalists, who retreated to Taiwan.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Factors: </strong>Many people were <a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/articles/zds2qfr#:~:text=In%20the%20early%201800s%2C%20the,treaties%20that%20harmed%20the%20Qing." target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">unhappy with the Qing dynasty</a>. Foreign invasions, internal rebellions, and social inequality caused problems and led to revolutionary movements. Sun’s Three Principles, Marxism-Leninism, and Maoism brought forth the changes in politics and society. Military struggle, civil war, and political mobilization were major factors in uniting the nation and strengthening the Communist Party's power.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 10px 0;"><strong>Challenges: </strong>Despite its successes, such as its economic growth and rise as a major world power, the country still faces numerous challenges, especially in the realm of political dissent, which is tightly controlled. There are other concerns persisting over Taiwan’s status, ethnic minority rights, and social inequalities in the country. China faces the challenge of balancing rapid modernization with environmental sustainability and social pressures.</p>
</mj-text>
